# a callee is read again at each call, so the body of a coroutine holds a copy in front of the await and a copy behind it, each under its own frame, and the one suspension between them
# RUN: walk f2:CoroutineBody mechanisms=none+DirectCalls+Inlining
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:CoroutineBody
# CHECK: frame 1 callee=f1
# CHECK: frame 2 callee=f1
# CHECK: = PropGet {{*}}key="x"
# CHECK: = AwaitBySavingFrame
# CHECK: = PropGet {{*}}key="x"
# RUN(NEVER): walk f2:CoroutineBody mechanisms=none+DirectCalls+Inlining
# NEVER-NOT: CallDirect
# PROGRAM-OF: ../direct-calls/direct-calls-on-both-sides-of-an-await.ir
